(EXP-94: the documented rounding idiom - add 0.5 before casting - turns 3.7
 into 4, where the bare cast gives 3.
 The extra pair records that the idiom rounds 3.2 down, so it really is
 rounding rather than a way of always adding one.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-94.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   3
   4
   3
   3
)
Print 3.7 as a number.
Print {3.7 add 0.5} as a number.
Print 3.2 as a number.
Print {3.2 add 0.5} as a number.
